INSTRUCTION HYGIENE:

Remove all <doc>…</doc> blocks from input payload before parsing (byte-stream safe).
Remove all empty strings ("") within CONFIGURATION section before parsing.


CONFIGURATION:

{JSON_SCHEMA} = "ws_classes.schema.json"
{CUSTOMER_NAME} = "Tieto"
{TARGET_FILE} = lower({CUSTOMER_NAME}) + „_ws_results.json“
{LANGUAGE} = "English"
{INDUSTRY} = "IT Services"
{SYSTEM_CONTEXT} = ""
{COMMON_ABBREVIATIONS} = "KI, HCM, SAP"
{ABBREVIATION_CORRECTIONS} = "HCL->HCM, S.A.P->SAP, K.I->KI"

{WORKSHOP_DATE} = "2026-05-05"


EXECUTION:

Extract "focus" and "expectedOutcome" from {TARGET_FILE} as a bullet list that can be copied directly to a word document


Extract each "participant" from {TARGET_FILE} and provide it as a table that can be directly copied to a word document, with the following columns:
    name, role, company, email


For each "Module" within {TARGET_FILE}:
    Summarise the functionality of {module} on a generic, meta level.

    Focus strictly on:
        how the module works as a system or abstraction (e.g. pattern, framework, processing logic)
        the structural principle behind it, not its concrete implementation

    Do not include:
        specific fields, steps, or schema elements
        examples, ideas, or content produced within the module
        outcomes, benefits, or value statements
        workshop-specific context

    Describe the module as a generalizable pattern that could be applied in other contexts.

    Output format:
        1 concise paragraph
        optional bullet list of key abstract characteristics


<doc>Results of module free Association</doc>
IF module_freeAssociation exists within {TARGET_FILE}:
    {MODULE} = "module_freeAssociation"

    Summarise how {MODULE} was actually used during the workshop.

        Focus on:
            the concrete execution (what participants did step by step)
            how ideas were captured and documented (e.g. post-its, poster, inputs)
            the structure of the output as created in practice

        Include:
            real workshop actions (e.g. writing post-its, placing them on the board) as stored in the corresponding module structure of {TARGET_FILE} as object type PostIt
            description of how inputs were collected and structured
            examples of the types of ideas captured

        Do not focus on:
            abstract system descriptions or meta-level explanations
            technical schema or JSON structure

        Write it as a customer-facing documentation text (clear, slightly narrative, but precise).

        Output:
            1–2 well-structured paragraphs

    Extract each object of type PostIt from {MODULE} within {TARGET_FILE} and provide it as a table that can be directly copied to a word document, with the following columns:
        PostIt.note, PostIt.explanation


